[{"id":"ops-predict-siren","itemId":"logic-operators","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"The siren sounds when the alarm is armed, the door or the window is open, and no test is running. <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is drawn for you, and so are steps 0 and 1. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> needs <code class=\"nobreak\">armed</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> at 1 and <code class=\"nobreak\">test</code> at 0, all in the same step: steps 2, 3 and 5. In step 4 the alarm is armed and everything is open, but a test is running, so <code class=\"nobreak\">~test</code> is 0 and the siren stays quiet. In step 6 nobody has armed it, and in step 7 a test is running again.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"quiet-alarm-story","source":"hdl/level-01/quiet_alarm/quiet_alarm_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"step","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"armed","path":"quiet_alarm_tb.armed","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[6,"0"],[7,"1"]]},{"label":"door_open","path":"quiet_alarm_tb.door_open","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"0"],[2,"1"],[3,"0"],[4,"1"],[7,"0"]]},{"label":"window_open","path":"quiet_alarm_tb.window_open","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[3,"1"]]},{"label":"test","path":"quiet_alarm_tb.test","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[4,"1"],[5,"0"],[7,"1"]]},{"label":"opening","path":"quiet_alarm_tb.dut.opening","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"0"],[2,"1"]]},{"label":"siren","path":"quiet_alarm_tb.siren","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[2,"1"],[4,"0"],[5,"1"],[6,"0"]],"samples":["0","0","1","1","0","1","0","0"]}]},"answer":"siren","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"ops-fill-not","itemId":"logic-operators","role":"core","promptHtml":"The siren must stay quiet while <code class=\"nobreak\">test</code> is 1. Type the operator that goes in front of <code class=\"nobreak\">test</code>.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">~test</code> is 1 while <code class=\"nobreak\">test</code> is 0, and 0 while <code class=\"nobreak\">test</code> is 1. ANDed with the rest, it lets the siren sound only when no test is running. (<code class=\"nobreak\">!</code> gives the same result on a single bit, but this course uses <code class=\"nobreak\">~</code>, which also works on every bit of a vector.)</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-01/quiet_alarm/quiet_alarm.sv","firstLine":1,"totalLines":14,"before":["// Lesson 0.2's burglar alarm with one more input: while someone is testing","// the alarm, the siren stays quiet.","module quiet_alarm (","  input  logic armed,        // 1 when the alarm is switched on","  input  logic door_open,    // 1 while the door is open","  input  logic window_open,  // 1 while the window is open","  input  logic test,         // 1 while someone is testing the alarm","  output logic siren         // 1 to sound the siren",");","  logic opening;             // 1 when the door or the window is open","","  assign opening = door_open | window_open;"],"blankLine":{"left":"  assign siren   = armed & opening & ","right":"test;"},"after":["endmodule"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"// Lesson 0.2's burglar alarm with one more input: while someone is testing","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// the alarm, the siren stays quiet.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"quiet_alarm","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" armed,        ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 when the alarm is switched on","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" door_open,    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 while the door is open","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" window_open,  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 while the window is open","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" test,         ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 while someone is testing the alarm","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" siren         ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 to sound the siren","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" opening;             ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 when the door or the window is open","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" opening ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" door_open ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"|","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" window_open;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" siren   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" armed ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"&","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" opening ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"&","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":"test;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]},"after":[[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]]},"accept":["~","!"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The missing operator"},{"id":"ops-report-lut4","itemId":"logic-operators","role":"core","promptHtml":"Vivado built <code class=\"nobreak\">quiet_alarm.sv</code>, four operators on four inputs, for the Arty A7-100T. Below is the Primitives table of its Utilization report: one row for each kind of cell, with how many the design uses. A LUT4 is a LUT that uses four of its inputs.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the LUT4 row. <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> depends on four inputs, so its truth table has 16 rows, and one LUT4 holds them all: the OR, the NOT and both ANDs are inside it, and so is <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code>. The IBUF and OBUF rows are the pin buffers of lesson 0.3, one for each input and one for the output.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/quiet_alarm/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":180,"excerpt":["+----------+------+---------------------+","| Ref Name | Used | Functional Category |","+----------+------+---------------------+","| IBUF     |    4 |                  IO |","| OBUF     |    1 |                  IO |","| LUT4     |    1 |                 LUT |","+----------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"How many LUT4 cells did Vivado use for the whole alarm?","answer":"1","numeric":true},{"id":"ops-find-bug","itemId":"logic-operators","role":"core","promptHtml":"This alarm should sound when it is armed, the door or the window is open, and no test is running. Its testbench fails. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> uses <code class=\"nobreak\">&amp;</code>, so it is 1 only when the door and the window are both open. An open door alone never sounds the siren: the testbench's first failure is the armed alarm with only the door open, at 30 ns. With <code class=\"nobreak\">|</code>, either one is enough. The <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> line is right: it needs the alarm armed, something open and no test.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-01/quiet_alarm_bug/quiet_alarm_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// Lesson 0.2's burglar alarm with one more input: while someone is testing","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// the alarm, the siren stays quiet.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"quiet_alarm_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" armed,        ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 when the alarm is switched on","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" door_open,    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 while the door is open","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" window_open,  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 while the window is open","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" test,         ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 while someone is testing the alarm","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" siren         ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 to sound the siren","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" opening;             ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// 1 when the door or the window is open","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" opening ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" door_open ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"&","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" window_open;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" siren   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" armed ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"&","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" opening ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"&","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"~","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"test;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"bugLine":12,"fixLine":"assign opening = door_open | window_open;"},{"id":"ops-report-seven","itemId":"logic-operators","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">and7.sv</code> ANDs seven inputs together, one more than a LUT has. Vivado built it for the Arty A7-100T. Below is the Slice Logic table of its Utilization report. A slice is one of the small groups of LUTs and flip-flops the chip is built from, so the Slice LUTs row counts LUTs; Used is how many this design takes.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the Used column of the Slice LUTs row. A LUT has six inputs, so no single LUT can see all seven. Vivado splits the AND over more than one LUT and joins them, so that together they see every input. What pushed it past one LUT is the seventh input, not the number of <code class=\"nobreak\">&amp;</code> operators.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/and7/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":32,"excerpt":["+-------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+","|        Site Type        | Used | Fixed | Prohibited | Available | Util% |","+-------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+","| Slice LUTs              |    2 |     0 |          0 |     63400 | <0.01 |","|   LUT as Logic          |    2 |     0 |          0 |     63400 | <0.01 |","|   LUT as Memory         |    0 |     0 |          0 |     19000 |  0.00 |","| Slice Registers         |    0 |     0 |          0 |    126800 |  0.00 |","|   Register as Flip Flop |    0 |     0 |          0 |    126800 |  0.00 |","|   Register as Latch     |    0 |     0 |          0 |    126800 |  0.00 |","| F7 Muxes                |    0 |     0 |          0 |     31700 |  0.00 |","| F8 Muxes                |    0 |     0 |          0 |     15850 |  0.00 |","| Unique Control Sets     |    0 |       |          0 |     15850 |  0.00 |","+-------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+"],"ask":"How many LUTs did Vivado use for and7?","answer":"2","numeric":true},{"id":"ops-predict-mixed","itemId":"logic-operators","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"In <code class=\"nobreak\">quiet_alarm</code>, the siren sounds when the alarm is armed, the door or the window is open, and no test is running. <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is not drawn. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> for every step.","explanationHtml":"<p>Only steps 1, 4 and 5 have the alarm armed, a door or window open, and no test. Step 0 and step 6 have a test running, step 2 has nothing open, step 3 is not armed, and in step 7 everything is off. <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is still there inside the alarm: you worked it out in your head as the door or the window.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"quiet-alarm-mixed","source":"hdl/level-01/quiet_alarm/quiet_alarm_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"step","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"armed","path":"quiet_alarm_tb.armed","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[3,"0"],[4,"1"],[7,"0"]]},{"label":"door_open","path":"quiet_alarm_tb.door_open","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"0"],[3,"1"],[6,"0"]]},{"label":"window_open","path":"quiet_alarm_tb.window_open","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[2,"0"],[3,"1"],[5,"0"],[6,"1"],[7,"0"]]},{"label":"test","path":"quiet_alarm_tb.test","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"0"],[6,"1"],[7,"0"]]},{"label":"siren","path":"quiet_alarm_tb.siren","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[2,"0"],[4,"1"],[6,"0"]],"samples":["0","1","0","0","1","1","0","0"]}]},"answer":"siren"}]